  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Bring a large saucepan of salted water to the boil for the pasta. Finely chop the onion. Finely chop the oregano leaves, discarding the stems (see Make it yours). Crush or finely chop the garlic.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2883502/photos/large/prep_ingredients-89077bf1ca5e4c6f6e940f1cd98f9ddb.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Brown mushroom meat: Heat 3 tsp olive oil in a medium deep frypan over medium heat. Cook the onion and garlic, stirring, for 3 mins or until softened. Add the mushroom meat and half the Italian seasoning and cook, stirring constantly and breaking up the lumps with a spoon, for 3 mins or until browned.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2883503/photos/large/cook_pasta-fc152639dbab70c7b4247e2e4723dec3.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer ragu: Add the tomatoes, half the tomato paste, 1 tbs soy sauce, 2 tsp sugar and 60ml (¼ cup) water to the mushroom meat mixture and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to medium and cook for 15 mins or until slightly thickened.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2883504/photos/large/brown_mushroom_meat-c568cd33e841f58d56fb571a9e4b9629.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook pasta: When the ragu is almost finished cooking, add the pasta to the pan of boiling water and cook, stirring to separate the strands, for 2-3 mins until al dente. Drain.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2883505/photos/large/simmer_ragu-23012c19ded0cbae6024f3c14bf4a46b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the pasta and oregano to the ragu and cook, stirring, for 1-2 mins until warmed through. Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper. Divide the ragu pasta among bowls and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2883506/photos/large/serve_up-b50f36851745885f186cf42aec74faa8.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: Reserve a few oregano sprigs if you like the rustic look in our photo, then scatter over the ragu before serving.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2883507/photos/large/make_it_yours-a83982b3c4392efd810c54d6d6542a24.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
